  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Polynesian Villas &amp; Bungalows are best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want a monorail to Magic Kingdom and a fifth bed in a studio,</strong> without booking a hotel room. Official 2026 listings put these longhouse Deluxe Studios at five adults.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups who specifically want a bungalow on the water.</strong> They sleep eight and look at the lagoon. They are priced in a different range than a studio.</li>
      <li><strong>People who already like the Polynesian and want a kitchenette or a full bungalow kitchen</strong> on the same monorail loop. <span class="verify">[verify bungalow kitchen layout]</span></li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You meant to book Island Tower.</strong> Duo Studios, Tower Deluxe Studios, tower villas and penthouses are on the <a href="/resorts/island-tower-resort/">Island Tower</a> page. A Tower Deluxe Studio sleeps four, not five.</li>
      <li><strong>The bungalow rate is a shock after looking at studios.</strong> In 2026 a bungalow ran about $3,662 to $7,045 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
      <li><strong>You want a standalone villa resort with no hotel next door.</strong> This is still the Polynesian campus, with the same crowds at the monorail and the main pool.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

  <section id="rooms">
    <h2>Room types, sizes and beds</h2>
    <p>This guide covers the longhouse Deluxe Studios and the bungalows at Disney's Polynesian Villas &amp; Bungalows. <a href="/resorts/island-tower-resort/">Island Tower</a> and the hotel rooms at <a href="/resorts/polynesian-village-resort/">Polynesian Village</a> have their own pages. Guests share the monorail, the boat dock and the hotel restaurants. Studios typically have a kitchenette. There is no extra-adult charge up to the occupancy limit.</p>
